 "procedure": [
  "The Phase A K2 builds' final ISA (DESIGN_BC 9.1), recorded BEFORE any Phase B / C kernel edit; test_compile.py::test_k2_tensor_isa_unchanged compares every core='tensor' build with it.",
  "Digest: sha256 of the build's *final_isa.s (FLYDSL_DUMP_IR) with every whole-word occurrence of its kernel symbol replaced by '<kernel>' (test_compile.isa_digest).",
  "Compile: GPU-less, COMPILE_ONLY=1 FLYDSL_RUNTIME_ENABLE_CACHE=0 FLYDSL_DUMP_IR=1 FLYDSL_GPU_ARCH=gfx950 ARCH=gfx950, layer.build(key)(*layer.ABI.zeros()) for each of test_compile.BUILDS (widths 1..8, the two fault builds, the S=8 debug build). Deterministic: two runs, same hashes.",
  "Recorded 2026-10-20 from a clean checkout of okorzh/muse-spark-amd-mono at ca9640e2e2 (git status empty), in muse-mono-dev:df3bd094 via /home/okorzh/muse-mono/bin/cpu_bc.sh; the resources equal the Phase A STATUS compile table.",
  "Regenerate ONLY when the toolchain changes (the test skips while 'toolchain' differs from the image's) and ONLY from the Phase A K2 sources: a tree whose vllm/models/muse_spark/amd/specialized_decode/mono/ is ca9640e2e2's (git worktree add <dir> ca9640e2e2, plus the image's compiled vllm/*.so as bin/cpu_bc.sh mounts them), with this test_compile.py copied in: python3 tests/models/muse_spark/amd_specialized_decode/test_compile.py --write-baseline <source> <image>. Never regenerate from a tree with B / C kernel edits: the test would then pass vacuously."
 ],
